# ccproteus machine-local overrides. Copy to local.sh and edit.
#
# This is the single seam where a host's own tooling opts into optional
# behavior without ccproteus carrying any knowledge of that tooling. It is
# gitignored and never ships: a fresh install has no local.sh, every opt-in
# below defaults off, and no tracked source names any host's layout.
#
# Trust: this file is executable zsh, sourced by ccproteus in its own process.
# It grants no privilege beyond writing ccproteus.sh beside it. A bug here is a
# host configuration error; ccproteus does not manage the user's shell startup.

# ── Context windows ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each profile owns manual and discovered limits in its .conf file.
# `ccproteus probe <profile>` reads metadata without inference by default.
# Context sizing is automatic; existing manual limits are preserved on upgrade.
# Legacy registry import uses model-registry (or model-registry.conf) under the
# state root; there is no separate registry-path setting.

# ── Pre-launch step ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An executable run as `<exe> prelaunch <cwd>` before each Claude launch, with
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR set to the launching profile. For host state that must be in
# place before Claude reads its config. Output is discarded, it is killed after
# 10s, and a failure never blocks the launch.
# export CCPROTEUS_PRELAUNCH="$HOME/.local/bin/my-prelaunch"

# ── Reaching a private endpoint ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to set here. ccproteus ships no transport: start your bridge's local
# proxy and export HTTPS_PROXY for the command, e.g.
#   HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:<port> ccproteus run <profile>
# ccproteus passes that value through unchanged to every network consumer.
